## NOT moved — the actual subject of the original question

| | repos | change |
|---|---|---|
| `.clj` sources — the JVM is the runtime | **954** | **none** |
| third-party JVM jar in top-level `:deps` | **149** | **none** |
| JVM build toolchain | **292** | **none** |

Chicory: 3 call sites, all inside the frozen inventory — the one class the cutover
contract calls forbidden has **zero breaches**, and that was unmeasured before this
session.

`:jvm-test` fleet gates went 56 -> 86. That is NOT backsliding: the additions are
other sessions gating repositories that had no gate at all. Coverage expanded.

## The one thing still unanswered

`io-ipld-car` was switched to `:nbb-test` + `:ship-git-deps true` as a canary for the
new classpath (be6780a). **It has not been exercised yet, and the reason is timing,
not a defect.**

The first reading of this was wrong and is corrected here. It looked as though two
ticks had run after the merge without producing a receipt, which would have meant a
declaration change does not trigger a re-run — a real hole in what ADR-2608137000
added. It is not that. The three `tick done` lines after the merge are BATCHES of one
tick that began its preflight at 02:30:27Z, thirteen minutes before the canary merged
at 02:43:11Z; a full tick takes roughly twenty-eight minutes here. That run read the
old gates.edn.

Checked rather than assumed:

    decl-hash of the entry now      81415915e2c85be7
    ~/.gftd/fleet-ci-state.edn      0ff73e8d7bb08950, :at 2026-08-16T13:39:57Z

The hash differs, so `changed?` will fire, and the state was NOT silently backfilled
with the new hash — which is the failure that would have hidden this. The next tick to
START will select it.

Expected when it runs: `exit 0`, `Ran 19 tests containing 64 assertions`, 0 failures —
the same numbers the fleet's own JVM receipt recorded on 2026-08-16, and the same
numbers this repo produced locally at the TIP with the derived classpath and
`npm install`.

To answer it deliberately rather than waiting:

    nbb --classpath '.:scripts/nbb_compat' scripts/fleet-ci/tick.cljs

If it goes red, the entry carries its own reading: exit 95 = npm install failed on the
node, 93/94 = no summary / zero tests, `Could not find namespace` in the output =
`ship-git-deps!` did not place something the classpath names. Revert is the entry back
to `:gate :jvm-test :cd true`.

Seven more gates measured clean for the same treatment and were deliberately NOT
switched until the canary answers: kotobase-lake 77/259, kotobase-protocols 66/238,
kotobase-protocol-core 24/97, org-apache-avro 14/32, org-apache-tinkerpop-gremlin
23/37, org-graphql-http 23/39, sakkyokuka 6/15.

## Owed, in priority order

1. **`.clj` sources, 954 repos.** The body. Port to `.cljc`, or lift the decision core
   to `.kotoba` per ADR-2608650000's split between a permanent safety constraint and a
   backend that has not caught up. Nothing else on this list reduces the JVM debt.
2. **third-party JVM jars, 149 repos.** cheshire / http-kit / ring-core / datalevin /
   transit-clj have no cljs form; each needs a real substitute decision.
3. **390 CLEAN-but-not-self-contained repos** — the runner tranche's next slice. The
   pipeline exists; they need a classpath built from `clojure -Spath`.
4. **14 real REDs** — repos green on the JVM and failing under ClojureScript:
   `mst` 262 errors, `glyph` 49 failures, `katex` 37, `arxiv` 14, `org-ros` 5+10,
   `mamori` 11, `media` 5.
5. **1,134 MIDDLE** (unknown until run) and **169 FLOOR** (definitely not portable).
6. **bb.edn `:complex` 167** — hand ports; do not point `emit-batch` at them.
7. Individually blocked: `isic-6492` needs a Worker-environment edge runner (6 ns);
   `kotobase-peer` has 5 pre-existing errors in `kotobase-projection`'s cljs half
   before its 2 can be added; `kobo` needs a second general runner; 3 bb repos need
   `System/getProperty` / `cljs.core/ExceptionInfo` made portable first.

## Known holes in the tools themselves

- `verify-cljs-runner-completeness` can call a runner complete when it uses
  `run-all-tests` with a REGEX filter that excludes a loaded namespace. Not hit today.
- Both detectors read local checkouts. The 438 landings were invisible to them until
  `west update` synced 390 checkouts; that is recorded in ADR-2608170500 and the
  session did run the sync.
- The `:nbb-test` node-side path is unverified end to end (the canary above).

## The failure that recurred, for the next reader

Five times today a stale local ref or an unchecked exit code produced a confident wrong
answer: `git archive` writing nothing into an unfetched checkout and being reported as
`NO-TEST-DIR-ON-MAIN` for 32 of 37 rows; `Ran 0 tests` classified as PASS; a stale
remote-tracking ref reporting `bb.edn` still present on three repos and then on 174;
`xargs -a` printing usage on BSD and being read as a completed `west update`.

Every one of those was OUTSIDE a tool. The scripts that were given an explicit check —
fetch before judging, an evidence floor, a distinct exit code for could-not-measure —
did not make the mistake once. The discipline this workspace writes into its detectors
is not applied to the commands typed next to them."

  :adr/consequences
  "- 438 repositories, 3,412 tests / 34,612 assertions, and six reusable scripts land.
- The JVM debt is unchanged and remains the subject: 954 `.clj`-source repos and 149
  third-party jars.
- One canary is outstanding; the command that answers it is in this ADR.
- No worktrees, branches, or stashes of this session remain. Nothing belonging to
  another session was moved."

